@startuml arch-serialization
' The two model-persistence paths and why both exist: the NATIVE path is fast but
' welds the file to one dictionary backend; the PORTABLE path is backend-agnostic
' and rebuilds the trie through a caller-supplied factory on load.
' Colour legend (semantic, shared across all repo diagrams — see architecture.puml):
'   #1565C0 blue = statistical LM core   #00838F teal = storage / persistence
'   #546E7A grey = external crates / corpora
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/arch-serialization.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 3 in docs/architecture/data-flow.md §6
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #EF6C00
title Model persistence — the native path vs. the portable path

rectangle "**In-memory model**\nNgramModel<D>  ·  HybridLanguageModel<D>" as model #1565C0

package "NATIVE  —  save / load   (feature: serde-extras)" {
  rectangle "**serde::Serialize on D**\nthe dictionary's own node graph, written verbatim" as native_ser #00838F
  rectangle "**bincode**\ncompact binary framing" as native_bin #00838F
  rectangle "**model.bin**\n**D-specific** — loadable only back into the //same// backend" as native_file #00838F
}

package "PORTABLE  —  save_portable / load_portable" {
  rectangle "**to_portable()**\nflatten the trie to (key, NgramEntrySnapshot) pairs\n— plain fields, because atomics cannot cross a serializer" as port_flat #1565C0
  rectangle "**PortableModel**\npairs + discounts + <latex>|V|</latex> + total count\n**no backend type appears in the schema**" as port_struct #1565C0
  rectangle "**model.portable.bin**\nloadable into **any** MutableMappedDictionary" as port_file #00838F
  rectangle "**dictionary_factory**\na caller-supplied closure that mints the backend\n//at load time//" as factory #546E7A
}

rectangle "**Rehydrated model**\nNgramModel<D'> — possibly a **different** backend" as rehydrated #1565C0

model --> native_ser : save
native_ser --> native_bin
native_bin --> native_file
native_file -[#00838F,dashed]-> model : load\n(same D only)

model --> port_flat : save_portable
port_flat --> port_struct
port_struct --> port_file
port_file --> factory : load_portable
factory --> rehydrated : replay pairs\ninto a fresh trie

note right of port_flat
  **Why a snapshot type exists.** NgramEntry's fields
  are AtomicU64 / AtomicU32, and an atomic has no
  meaningful serialized identity. NgramEntrySnapshot is
  the Copy plain-field twin, taken with Relaxed loads at
  a quiescent point.
end note

note right of factory
  **The escape hatch.** Train once over a mutable
  DynamicDawgChar, ship the portable file, then load into
  a read-optimized DoubleArrayTrieChar in production —
  no retraining, no format migration.
end note

@enduml
